'''San Hill''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Muun]] and [[Chairman]] of the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. He pledged the support of the Banking Clan to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and served as the financial cartel's representative on the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]]. Hill and the rest of the council were [[Mission to Mustafar|slaughtered]] by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] on [[Mustafar]] following the end of the Clone Wars.

==Biography==
[[File:SanHill-SWM43.png|thumb|left|270px|San Hill pledges the financial support of the Banking Clan to the newly formed Confederacy of Independent Systems.]]
A [[Gender|male]] [[Muun]] from the [[planet]] [[Scipio]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> San Hill was the [[President]]<ref name="Creatures">''[[Créatures et peuples de la galaxie]]''</ref> and [[Chairman]] of the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]], also known as the IGBC.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> He was one of the richest Muuns in [[the galaxy]] yet constantly sought to increase his wealth.<ref name="Creatures" /> At some point, Hill attempted to assassinate [[General]] [[Grievous]],<ref name="Star Wars: Masterwork">{{Topps|set=2019 Topps Star Wars Masterwork|cardname=General Grievous}}</ref> a [[Kaleesh]] [[warlord]] who had previously allied himself with<ref name="The Separatists">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Separatists}}</ref> the Banking Clan as an [[agent]]<ref name="Battle Droids Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Droids and Other Droids of War}}</ref> because of his grudge towards the [[Jedi]] and the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]].<ref name="The Separatists" /> Grievous would survive a [[Sabotage of Grievous' shuttle|shuttle crash]] and be rebuilt as a [[cyborg]].<ref name="HC 8">[[Star Wars Helmet Collection 8|''Star Wars Helmet Collection'': General Grievous]]</ref>

On the onset of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="San Hill" /> Hill attended a secret meeting on [[Geonosis]]<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> and signed a [[Geonosian accord|treaty]] with [[Count]] [[Dooku]]'s [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="San Hill" /> pledging the Banking Clan's financial and military assets to the movement<ref name="Base Series 1">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=San Hill - Banking Clan Chairman}}</ref> in a non-exclusive deal;<ref name="HC 23">{{HelmetCollectionCite|23|Databank A-Z}}</ref> the banks would continue to do business with the Republic to reap profits from both factions in the coming war,<ref name="Pursuit of Peace">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref> albeit with a pro-Separatist leaning in truth.<ref name="HC 59">{{HelmetCollectionCite|59|Databank A-Z}}</ref>

Hill served as the financial cartel's representative on the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]].<ref name="San Hill" /> During the final [[Standard day|days]] of the Clone Wars, Hill, along with the other Separatist leaders, moved from [[Utapau]] to [[Mustafar]]<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref> where they were all [[Death|killed]] by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

==Personality and traits==
Like most Muuns, San Hill was more comfortable with business and closed-door [[politics]] than being on the front lines of war. Hill was highly influential, and wasn't above conspiring with others to get his way.<ref name="Base Series 1" /> As Chairman of the IGBC, Hill believed that no war could be fought without money.<ref name="San's Card">{{ForceCollection|San Hill|star=4}}</ref>

A male Muun, Hill stood at 1.91 [[meter]]s tall,<ref name="San Hill" /> and had [[Color|yellow]] [[eye]]s and pale skin.<ref name="Attack of the Clones" />

==Behind the scenes==
San Hill first appeared in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], the second installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[prequel trilogy]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> Hill then appeared once more in [[2005]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> The character was designed by concept artist [[Dermot Power]]. One of the designs featured the character with light-blue skin and wearing dark clothes and another,<ref name="ArtofII">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode II: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref> with the production code "dp478",<ref name="DPower">{{WebCite|url=https://dermotpower.com/star-wars-episode-2attack-of-the-clones|text=Star Wars Episode 2:Attack of the Clones|work=[[Dermot Power]]'s website|archivedate=20260211111619}}</ref> featured him with ash-grey skin and grey clothing.<ref name="ArtofII" /> In the film, Hill was realized as a computer generated character.<ref name="databank">{{DB|character|sanhill|Hill, San}}</ref> Though Hill's death was never depicted onscreen during ''Revenge of the Sith'',<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> the [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay|illustrated screenplay]] indicates that Hill was killed just before [[Poggle the Lesser]].<ref name="Ep. III Illustrated Screenplay">[[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay'']]</ref> The [[2015]] [[canon]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'' confirmed his death.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

According to one ''[[Star Wars: Card Trader]]'' release, Hill conspired with [[Poggle the Lesser]], the [[Archduke]] of Geonosis, and Dooku to destroy their volatile ally Grievous, whom they could then rebuild as a super-[[cyborg]] of servitude.<ref name="Base Series 1" /> [[Pablo Hidalgo]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] asked fans to disregard this detail as an outdated Legends reference.<ref name="Lost Pablo Tweet">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/672253588018618368|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=Tweet lost, but did state that San Hill - Banking Clan Chairman - ''Base Series 1'' contains an outdated reference to Legends via San Hill, Poggle, and Dooku working together to destroy and rebuild Grievous.|nobackup=1}}</ref> However, other canon sources have brought in similar details.<ref name="HC 8" />

